[#:seon.task{:name "no-auth-refuses-at-complete"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent overlay with `:seon.config.ai/no-auth` true and a model with no descriptor row makes every turn fail at the provider call: configured-targets dissociates `:seon.ai/api-key-variable`, then `seon.ai/complete`'s contract requires it (\"refused argument 1 at [`:seon.ai/api-key-variable`] ... Called from `seon.turn/call-turn`\"), fault d31e076c on default 2026-09-27. The agent test's local provider relies on the same dials. Either complete's contract admits a target without a key when no-auth holds, or no-auth is refused where it is configured."
             :must-read #{seon.ai/complete seon.ai/targets}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-ai-test-captured-run4-reply-is-unread"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "The ai-test captured-run4 reply is unread (\"Unmatched delimiter\"): the reader/planned-sources owner. Done when the captured source reads and the test is green, or the reader's refusal names the delimiter's position."
             :must-read #{seon.ai/attempt-ai}}
 #:seon.task{:name "deepseek-model-rows-and-dial-classification-are-stale"
             :kind :schema
             :intent "DeepSeek check 2026-10-07 (tmp/deepseek/report.md, provider pages and live GET /models): the deepseek-flash id and request shape are right, but (1) the deepseek-v4-pro row (config/default.edn ~545-558) carries old prices (0.435/0.003625/0.87, now 0.66/0.022/1.98 off-peak) and daily off-peak window refs that do not match the weekday-only peak schedule; (2) the flash row understates context (1000000 vs 1048576) and max output (384000 vs 393216); (3) :top_p is classified inert-when-thinking (resources/seon/schemas/seon.config.ai.edn ~155-158) although the provider honours it ONLY in thinking mode; (4) docs/seon/reference/llm-adapters.md:77 still shows deepseek-v4-flash; (5) `:seon.config.ai/prompt-token-budget` is 1,000,000 while the window is 1,048,576 and max_tokens ships 65,536, so a full prompt plus output can exceed the window (unverified at the REPL). Done when the rows and the top_p classification match the provider facts, the doc is current, and the prompt budget plus configured max output fits the configured model's window (checked where the budget is read), before loop S1's paid pass. Proof: a new seon.ai-test/configured-prompt-budget-and-output-fit-the-model-window (to be written first) naming this task, over the shipped config/default.edn rows."
             :must-read #{seon.ai/request-body}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/deepseek--report.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-dsml-tool-call-reply-reads-as-prose"
             :kind :function
             :intent "deepseek-flash answered 7 of 32 fan-out 5 replies (default 6e4d7a341, :chat wire format, 2026-10-09) (fan-out 6 on 6e9b9017c, after the alias fix: 5 of 30) with its native tool-call markup ('<｜｜DSML｜｜ calls> <｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=...>') instead of Clojure forms, after a form failed on an unresolved alias; the reply read as prose (no form), or its closing tags as symbols ('Unable to resolve symbol: </invoke>'), and the run ended waiting. Done when such a reply is answered with a typed reply error naming the markup and telling the model to write the call as a Clojure form, asserted on reply data."
             :must-read #{seon.ai/request-body seon.turn/continuing-reply?}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-output-observed?"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Give `seon.ai/output-observed?` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it (`docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`): registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, file a task on the producer naming `seon.ai/output-observed?` in its must-read with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower."
             :must-read #{seon.ai/output-observed? seon.contracts/gaps}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md"}}]
